<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  org.ruyaos.Update1 — OS image updates: check, stage (as a download job that can be paused,
  resumed and cancelled), roll back, choose the channel.
  Service: ruya-update on the system bus at /org/ruyaos/Update1 (over bootc, T-151); the shell's
  mock backend follows the same rules.
  Contract between shell (Qt/QML) and services (Rust); see docs/specs/01-platform.md §4.

  The user restarts from the shell (logind, Power.restart) once the state is "staged".

  Schedule (T-154, the service decides, nobody has to open Settings):
    - It checks when it starts (if the last finished check is older than 24 h) and then every
      24 h (a failed scheduled check is retried after an hour). A scheduled check that finds an
      update downloads it; a check the user started with Check does not.
    - A staged image is booted by the service itself, with `systemctl reboot`, when the setting
      auto_restart is on, the local time is between 03:00 and 05:00, the console has had no
      input for 30 minutes and no app runs. Idle time and apps come from the shell through
      ReportActivity; with no report since the service started, idle time counts from the start.
    - Notice (T-159): when those rules first hold the service does not restart at once. It sets
      restart_at to now + 120 s and emits StatusChanged; the shell tells the user. At a look at the
      schedule (once a minute) at or after restart_at, if the rules still hold, it restarts. Any
      ReportActivity, SetAutoRestart(false), or the image no longer being staged clears restart_at
      (StatusChanged) and the 30 idle minutes start again. The restart lands 120 to 180 s after
      the notice.
    - A scheduled download that failed is tried again after an hour (as a failed scheduled check);
      a download the user started with Download is not retried.
    - A download the download policy paused (the job's reason "playing", RUY-31) runs again by
      itself at the next look at the schedule once ReportActivity says no app runs; one the user
      paused waits for ResumeDownload or Download. A scheduled check that finds the update a
      paused download is for continues it.

  Status strings (the reply of every method) are stable API:
    "ok"           success: Check and Download only start the work, progress arrives with
                   StatusChanged
    "busy"         a check or download is already running (Rollback: also while staging)
    "unavailable"  nothing to do: Download without an update found, Rollback without
                   rollback_available
    "invalid"      malformed argument (SetChannel with an unknown channel)
    "forbidden"    Rollback, SetChannel or SetAutoRestart from a caller that is not an admin
                   (see below)
    "failed"       internal error
    "wrong-state"  PauseDownload with nothing downloading, ResumeDownload with no download paused,
                   CancelDownload with no download running or paused
    "unsupported"  PauseDownload or CancelDownload once the image's import has begun (the job's
                   resumable is false): a half-imported deployment is never left behind

  Admin: Rollback, SetChannel and SetAutoRestart are for an admin. The shell asks for the admin's PIN first and
  checks it with Profiles1.VerifyAdmin; the bus policy lets only ruya-shell and root call this
  interface. Decided (lead, 2026-10-30): the service does not take a PIN, but it checks the caller
  the way ruya-store checks AddRemote (root, or ruya-shell while Profiles1's active profile is an
  admin) and answers "forbidden" otherwise.

  Status record (a{sv}), keys (GetStatus):
    state             s   "idle" | "checking" | "downloading" | "staged" | "up-to-date" | "failed"
                          idle        nothing running (an update may be waiting: see available;
                                      also while the download is paused)
                          checking    looking for a newer image
                          downloading staging the new image (progress 0..100)
                          staged      the next boot uses `staged`: the shell offers a restart
                          up-to-date  the last check found nothing newer
                          failed      the last check or download failed (see error)
    current           s   running image version, e.g. "0.0.18"
    available         s   version a check found and Download would stage, "" when none
    staged            s   version that will boot next (also after a rollback), "" when none
    channel           s   "stable" | "beta"
    auto_restart      b   restart by itself into a staged image when the console is idle at night
                          (default true)
    last_check        x   unix seconds of the last finished check, 0 = never (kept over restarts)
    restart_at        x   unix seconds at which the service restarts by itself, 0 = no restart
                          is announced (T-159). Only set while state is "staged" and auto_restart
                          is true; the shell shows a notice while it is non-zero.
    progress          u   the download job's percent, 0..100 (meaningful while downloading or
                          paused)
    rollback_available b  a previous image exists that Rollback can boot
    error             s   short text of the last failure, "" otherwise

  Unknown keys are ignored by clients. The record is re-read after every StatusChanged.

  The download job (ADR-026, RUY-29). Download stages the image as one job, the "image job": the
  ADR-026 v2 record that Store1 serves for its jobs, with source "update", kind "os", app "",
  position 0 and title "RuyaOS <version>". There is at most one: GetDownloadJob and JobChanged
  give the running or paused one, else the last that finished since the service started.

  Byte source: `bootc upgrade|switch --progress-fd` (bootc 1.17.1; a pipe, a file is refused)
  writes JSON lines: one "Start", then "ProgressBytes" about ten times a second while layers are
  fetched (bytes of this run, bytesTotal still to fetch, bytesCached already present, the same in
  layers as steps), then "ProgressSteps" for the import and the deploy, which carry no bytes.
  Another event type is ignored, a line that is no event is skipped (the job goes on). Measured
  on the Dell, 0.0.105 -> 0.0.106: 21 s without an event, 114 s of bytes, about 80 s of import,
  12 s of deploy.

  Pause and resume: PauseDownload stops bootc (SIGTERM). Layers fully fetched before it stay in
  the OSTree repository, also over a reboot, and the next run reuses them (more layers cached,
  fewer to fetch); only the layer in flight is fetched again. ResumeDownload runs the same
  command again, and Download does the same while the job is paused. A paused job survives a
  service restart (kept in the state directory): it comes back paused, with `available` set to
  its version. CancelDownload ends it for good: nothing is staged, the booted and rollback
  deployments are untouched, and the fetched layers are left to bootc's own cleanup. SetChannel
  and Rollback end a paused job as cancelled (it was for the other channel, or would stage the
  newer image over the rollback).

  Job record (a{sv}), keys (GetDownloadJob, JobChanged):
    id           s   "os-<unix seconds it began>" (a "-2" suffix when the last job had that id);
                     the same over a pause and resume
    source       s   "update"
    kind         s   "os"
    app          s   "" (the image is no app)
    title        s   "RuyaOS <version>": the version the check found (or the channel switched to)
    state        s   "running" | "paused" | "finished"
    status       s   "" unless finished, then "ok" (staged), "failed" or "cancelled"
    reason       s   "" | "playing" (paused by the download policy, not by the user;
                     ResumeDownload clears it)
    phase        s   "download" (layers arrive: ProgressBytes) | "install" (the import and the
                     deploy: ProgressSteps); "download" while paused
    percent      u   bytes_done * 90 / bytes_total while fetching (capped at 90), then 90..95 over
                     the first install task (the import) and 95..99 over the later ones (the
                     deploy), 100 when staged; never decreasing within the job, over a pause and
                     resume too
    bytes_done   t   bytes fetched over the network for this job, all its runs added up (what
                     GetDownloadStats counts; after a resume it can exceed bytes_total, because
                     the layer in flight at the pause is fetched again)
    bytes_total  t   bytesTotal of the job's first ProgressBytes (what was still to fetch then),
                     fixed for the job; 0 = unknown (no ProgressBytes yet)
    rate_bps     t   smoothed rate: byte deltas sampled once a second, exponential smoothing with
                     a 5 s time constant; 0 after 10 s without a byte, 0 while not running, and
                     0 = unknown
    eta_s        u   while running in phase "download": (bytes_total - bytes_done) / rate_bps
                     rounded up; 0 = unknown (the rate or the total is 0, or the import runs:
                     its length is not reported)
    position     u   0 (the image job is never queued)
    resumable    b   PauseDownload is offered: true while not finished and in phase "download",
                     false from the import on
    started      x   unix seconds the job began
    finished     x   unix seconds it finished, 0 while not finished

  Download stats (GetDownloadStats): the bytes this service fetched, per local day, in a
  root-only ledger in the state directory, kept for 90 days. A run's bytes count on the day it
  ends (finished or paused).

  Day record (a{sv}), keys (GetDownloadStats):
    day      s   "YYYY-MM-DD", local time
    bytes    t   bytes this service fetched that day
    jobs     u   image jobs that finished that day, whatever their status
    failed   u   of those, the failed ones
-->
<node>
  <interface name="org.ruyaos.Update1">

    <!-- Starts a check for a newer image. state becomes "checking", then "idle" (available
         set) or "up-to-date" (or "failed"). -->
    <method name="Check">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Stages the image a check found, as a new image job. state becomes "downloading"
         (progress), then "staged". With a paused job it continues that job (as ResumeDownload),
         also when nothing is `available`. -->
    <method name="Download">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- The download (job phase "download") stops; the job is paused and the status record's
         state becomes "idle" with `available` still set. The reply comes at once, the pause
         when bootc has stopped (JobChanged, StatusChanged). "unsupported" once the import has
         begun; "wrong-state" when nothing is downloading (or a cancel is under way); "ok" again
         while a pause is under way. -->
    <method name="PauseDownload">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- The paused download runs again; already fetched layers are not fetched again.
         "wrong-state" when no download is paused; "busy" while a check runs. -->
    <method name="ResumeDownload">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- A running or paused download stops for good: the job finishes with status "cancelled",
         nothing is staged; fetched layers are left to bootc's cleanup. A paused job ends at
         once, a running one when bootc has stopped. During the import: "unsupported" (as
         PauseDownload). "wrong-state" when no download runs or is paused. -->
    <method name="CancelDownload">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- The image job's Job record (see the header): an empty dictionary when there has been
         none since the service started, else the current or last finished download. status is
         always "ok". -->
    <method name="GetDownloadJob">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
      <arg name="job" type="a{sv}" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Day records (see the header), one per local day, newest first, at most `days` (1..90),
         days without bytes left out. "invalid" for days 0 or above 90, "failed" when the ledger
         cannot be read (it is then left as it is and nothing more is counted). -->
    <method name="GetDownloadStats">
      <arg name="days" type="u" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
      <arg name="stats" type="aa{sv}" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Admin. Makes the previous image the next boot; state becomes "staged" with `staged` set.
         rollback_available is false afterwards. -->
    <method name="Rollback">
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Admin. channel is "stable" or "beta". Clears `available`: the next Check applies it. -->
    <method name="SetChannel">
      <arg name="channel" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Admin. Turns "Restart automatically for updates" on or off; stored by the service.
         Changes auto_restart in the record. -->
    <method name="SetAutoRestart">
      <arg name="enabled" type="b" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="status" type="s" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- The shell calls this when input arrives, at most once a minute, and at once when the
         first app starts or the last one closes, and says whether an app is running. It resets
         the idle time; while app_running was the last report, the console does not restart by
         itself. It also calls off an announced restart (restart_at becomes 0). Any caller the bus
         policy lets in may call it. No reply status. -->
    <method name="ReportActivity">
      <arg name="app_running" type="b" direction="in"/>
    </method>

    <method name="GetStatus">
      <arg name="status" type="a{sv}" direction="out"/>
    </method>

    <!-- Any field of the status record changed (also every progress step): read GetStatus. -->
    <signal name="StatusChanged"/>

    <!-- The image job's whole Job record, when it changed: on every state and phase change and
         at most once a second while it runs. StatusChanged fires with it (its `progress` is the
         job's percent). -->
    <signal name="JobChanged">
      <arg name="job" type="a{sv}"/>
    </signal>
  </interface>
</node>
